      "body": [
        {
          "md": "Qa5+ wins the pawn back, but Bd2 develops with tempo and after Qxe5 your queen is exposed in front of your own king. Trading queens with Qxd3 and then Nxe4 would have removed White's most dangerous pieces and kept your king safe."
        }
      ]
    },
    "eae3732d-38c1-45d6-9a1f-7aa536eafa28": {
      "kind": "critical_moment",
      "ply": 16,
      "body": [
        {
          "md": "Nxe4 grabs a knight but allows a forced mate: Qd8+ Kxd8 Bg5+ is a double check, and after Kc7 comes Bd8#. With your king in the centre and the file in front of it open, development came first. Be7 prepares castling and keeps the game going."
        }
      ]
    }
